{
  "summary": "Two root causes identified. (1) Slow initial load: The Go server renders the client page from in-memory state that only gets populated when the Python pipeline pushes a state_update via WebSocket (every 2s periodic broadcast). If the browser loads the page before the first push arrives, the page renders empty/stale and must wait up to 5 seconds for smartPollFeatures to fetch updated HTML. Fix: either have the Go server proactively request state from the pipeline on first page load, or add a client-side immediate poll on page load (call smartPollFeatures() immediately instead of only on a 5s interval). (2) New items not appearing: The create_idea flow is fire-and-forget — the Go server sends the command to the pipeline via WebSocket, returns 200 immediately, and the browser calls smartPollFeatures() right after. But the pipeline hasn't processed the idea yet (it needs to create the JSON file, reload features, and push state back). The single immediate poll races against this round-trip and almost always loses. Fix: after creating an idea, poll more aggressively (e.g., retry smartPollFeatures 3 times at 1-second intervals) or have the Go server wait for the next state_update from the pipeline before returning the create_idea response, confirming the item exists before the UI tries to render it."
}
